---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import { RATE_LIMIT } from '../content/proof';
import { LEGAL_UPDATED } from '../content/legal';

// Pagina descrie ce face site-ul, nu ce e plănuit. Aceeași variabilă decide și
// dacă beaconul se încarcă, în Site.astro, deci cele două nu pot ajunge să
// spună lucruri diferite. Au ajuns o dată: pagina anunța statistici care nu
// existau.
const analytics = Boolean(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN);

import { BOOKING } from '../content/booking';
import { PAGE_COUNTER } from '../content/counter';
import { paths } from '../i18n/routes';

const updated = LEGAL_UPDATED.privacy.en;

// This page describes what the site actually does, so it changes when the site
// does, and neither of the two switches above is read anywhere else by hand.
// Booking is on, so Calendly is listed here and the button is on both contact
// pages; the note that used to sit here said the opposite and had been wrong
// since the button came back. Analytics is off, and stays off: the beacon
// measures 10,264 bytes on the wire against 5,612 for the whole site, which
// would make the stamp on the home page false by a factor of nearly three.
// Traffic is counted on the server instead (functions/_middleware.ts, ADR-0006),
// by the host already named below, with no script, no cookie and no third
// party. PAGE_COUNTER decides whether the pages describe it.
const sections = [
	{
		title: 'Who processes the data',
		body: [
			'Quick Flow SRL, fiscal code 44089760, registered at Sos. Mihai Bravu 39, bl. P15, sc. A, et. 3, ap. 11, Sector 2, 021305 Bucharest, Romania. Write to alexandru@quickflow.dev with any question about your data.',
		],
	},
	{
		title: 'On what basis',
		body: [
			'Article 6(1)(b) of the GDPR: steps taken at your request before entering a contract. You write to find out whether we should work together, I process what you wrote so that I can answer you.',
			'Article 6(1)(f) for two things more. The first is keeping the form from being abused. The anti-robot check and the rule that counts submissions per IP address both read technical data to do their job, and that is not something you asked for. The legitimate interest is a contact form that still reaches me on the day somebody points a script at it.',
			...(PAGE_COUNTER
				? ['The second is counting page views. Knowing which pages are read and which sites send people here is how I decide what to write next, and the count is built so that it says nothing about who you are.']
				: []),
			'There is no consent box and you are not asked for one, because I do nothing with the data beyond answering you.',
		],
	},
	{
		title: 'What I collect',
		body: [
			'Only what you write in the contact form: your name, your email address, what the message is about, the description of the project, what you have now and a link to it if you give one, the budget range, when you want it, and how you got here. If it is about a payment flow, also the four short answers about who pays, who is paid, who takes a cut and when the work counts as delivered.',
			'I do not ask for and do not collect health data, beliefs, financial data or any other kind of sensitive data. If you write them into the description of your own accord they end up in my inbox, so avoid them.',
		],
	},
	{
		title: 'What I do with it',
		body: [
			'I answer you. That is all. I do not use it for advertising, I do not sell it, I do not pass it on, and I do not build a profile out of it.',
		],
	},
	{
		title: 'Where it goes',
		body: [
			'The form sends its contents by email, through Resend, to my address. If the submission passes the anti-robot check, a single copy also goes to the address you wrote. The site has no database and stores nothing on the server.',
			'The emails stay in my inbox for as long as the conversation makes sense, and at most three years after the last message, which is how long an agreement can be disputed under Romanian law. If you want them deleted sooner, write to me and I delete them.',
		],
	},
	{
		title: 'Who else sees the data, as a provider',
		body: [
			`Cloudflare, which hosts the site and runs the form function. Cloudflare Turnstile checks whether the submission comes from a person, and to do that it processes the IP address and technical signals about the browser. A rule at the edge also counts submissions per IP address and blocks more than ${RATE_LIMIT.posts} in ${RATE_LIMIT.seconds} seconds, which is what keeps the form from being a free mailer.`,
			'Resend, which delivers the email. It leaves from the European region of Resend, in Ireland.',
			'Cloudflare and Resend are American companies, so the data can be processed outside the European Economic Area. Both do that under the standard contractual clauses approved by the European Commission.',
			// CR-49. To be checked by a lawyer before publishing: the transfer basis for Mux, a DPA, and cookies.
			"Mux, which streams the showreel on the home page and on the Plate page. Nothing goes to Mux until you press Play. Then your browser fetches the video from Mux's servers, which see your IP address and the technical details any server sees when it sends a file. The player sends Mux no viewing statistics. Mux is an American company.",
			...(analytics
				? ['Cloudflare Web Analytics, which counts page views. It stores no cookie and builds no profile.']
				: []),
			...(PAGE_COUNTER
				? ['Cloudflare also counts page views, on its own servers and with no script in the page. For each page opened it records the address of the page, the name of the site you came from (google.com, for example, never the full link), your country as Cloudflare works it out from the connection, whether you use a phone or a computer, and whether the visit looks like a robot. It records no IP address, no cookie and no identifier, so two visits by the same person cannot be linked. The counts are kept for three months and then deleted.']
				: []),
			...(BOOKING
				? ['Calendly, but only if you choose to book a slot. What you type there is processed by them, under their own policy, and I only see the booking.']
				: []),
		],
	},
	{
		title: 'Cookies',
		body: [
			analytics
				? 'The site sets no cookies. Traffic statistics come from Cloudflare Web Analytics, which uses no cookies, sets no identifier and does not recognise you from one visit to the next. That is why you see no cookie banner.'
				: PAGE_COUNTER
					? 'The site sets no cookies and carries no analytics script. Page views are counted on the server, as described above, without cookies and without recognising you from one visit to the next. That is why you see no cookie banner.'
					: 'The site sets no cookies and carries no analytics script at all. That is why you see no cookie banner. If I add traffic statistics later it will be Cloudflare Web Analytics, which uses no cookies and does not identify individual visitors, and this page will say so on the day it goes live, not before.',
		],
	},
	{
		title: 'Your rights',
		body: [
			'You can ask to see what data I hold about you, to have it corrected, to have it deleted, to receive it in a form you can take elsewhere, to restrict the processing, or to object to it. Write to alexandru@quickflow.dev and I will deal with it. If you are not satisfied with how I dealt with it, you can complain to the Romanian data protection authority, ANSPDCP, or to the supervisory authority in your own country.',
		],
	},
	{
		title: 'If anything changes',
		body: [
			'I update this page and change the date below. There are no hidden versions and I send no notifications, so if it matters to you, check the date.',
		],
	},
];
---

<Site
	lang="en"
	title="Privacy policy | Quick Flow"
	description="What the form collects, where it goes, how long it is kept and how it can be deleted. No cookies, no advertising."
>
	<section class="bleed pt-12 md:pt-16">
		<div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-10 gap-y-3">
			<p class="spec">Privacy</p>
			<p class="spec">Updated {updated}</p>
		</div>

		<h1 class="display-xl mt-8 max-w-[16ch]">What happens to what you write here.</h1>

		<p class="lead mt-9 max-w-[54ch] text-lg">
			In short: what you write in the form reaches my inbox, so that I can answer you. The site has
			no database, sets no cookies and does not track you.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="bleed mt-32" aria-labelledby="policy">
		<h2 id="policy" class="sr-only">The policy</h2>

		<div class="flex flex-col">
			{
				sections.map((s, i) => (
					<article class="hair rise grid gap-4 py-9 md:grid-cols-12 md:gap-10 md:py-12">
						<p class="spec md:col-span-1 md:pt-2">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</p>
						<h3 class="display-md md:col-span-4">{s.title}</h3>
						<div class="md:col-span-6 md:col-start-7">
							{s.body.map((line, j) => (
								<p class:list={['prose-body max-w-[54ch]', j > 0 && 'mt-4']}>{line}</p>
							))}
						</div>
					</article>
				))
			}
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- The same closing plate the terms page has, because these two are
	     the same kind of page. The action is the one a privacy page
	     actually has: not "hire me", but "take it down". -->
	<section class="band mt-16 md:mt-20">
		<div class="bleed py-20 md:py-28">
			<div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-12">
				<h2 class="display-lg md:col-span-7">If you want what you wrote here deleted, say so and it is gone.</h2>
				<div class="md:col-span-4 md:col-start-9 md:self-end">
					<a href={paths.contact.en} class="btn btn-primary">Write to me</a>
					<p class="prose-body mt-6 max-w-[34ch] text-[0.95rem]">Answered the same working day. No form to fill in and no reason to give.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Site>
